      "touched_round": 0,
      "title": "Replace six vllm-lite skills with repo-native skills",
      "rationale": "The copied vllm-lite skills target a Rust codebase (cargo/clippy/just, crates/, RUST_LOG, vllm-testing) that does not exist here; leaving them would misdirect agents into running wrong commands. Rewrote five in place with this repos actual extension surfaces (MODEL_REGISTRY/core registries/TASK_REGISTRY/SOURCE_REGISTRY/BACKEND_REGISTRY, uv+make+pytest gates, tests/support conventions) and replaced add-kernel with add-task, which matches the repos most common extension path.",
      "alternatives_rejected": "(1) keep vllm-lite skills as-is: rejected — actively misleading; (2) delete without replacement: rejected — loses the workflow coverage the user wanted; (3) keep add-kernel name for a repo without kernels: rejected — renamed to add-task for discoverability",
      "body": "Scope: .agents/skills/{add-architecture,add-component,add-task,debug-inference,run-ci,write-test}; graph-engineering kept unchanged (repo-agnostic)"
    },
